From 1ae7b6af4cb5445014cd8c8161a765cc25323d7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: D-Ogi <6542335+D-Ogi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:41:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wsi/win32: KMT present path (D3DKMTPresent of a linear
 device-local image)

Win32 without a D3D runtime device: swapchain images are linear, dedicated,
device-local RADV images whose allocation carries the kernel driver's LB7A
surface description; the winsys presents them through D3DKMTPresent(Blt) on
a separate non-UMD context, ordered by GPU waits and signals on the common
blit timeline semaphore. No CPU copy, no DXGI, works inside processes that
ship their own dxgi.dll. Present log path 'kmt'. BC250_WSI_CPU_PRESENT=1
keeps the CPU path; the hosted ICD keeps it too (host version 5 has no
Present). BC250_WSI_KMT_DWMFLUSH=1 adds DwmFlush per present.
